WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
 - As I might've mentioned, so we,

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.060
 I'm an internal medicine physician.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.600
 I'm a primary care doctor.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.640
 And all along, I've been trained

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.020
 to treat hypertension a certain way.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.680
 And it turns out that that wasn't

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.120
 necessarily

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.120
 the correct way, right?

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.800
 We've been doing it wrong for many years.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.920
 And so I truly feel that this is an

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.840
 opportunity

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.520
 to revamp the way that we approach

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:24.960
 patients

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.280
 with hypertension.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.830
 It's very much a care team, a team-based

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.400
 model, right?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.420
 That is important for us to adopt

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.800
 across the city of Chicago,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.100
 no matter where you're getting your care

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:37.560
 from.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.940
 So I truly feel that that is an

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.440
 opportunity for our team

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.910
 to go into health centers on the south

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:43.760
 and west sides

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.040
 to really establish a standard of care

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.240
 as it relates to the treatment

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.800
 of patients with hypertension.

